], "best_idea":"A small progression engine on three numbers per item kind (a weight that rises each level, falls when one is generated, and a threshold that forces the kind when the run falls behind a depth schedule) gives stat growth at a predictable pace without a fixed script.", "decision":"adapt", "decision_why":"Take the rise-on-level, fall-on-spawn weight and the depth threshold for stat-growth tokens (life and strength), with a seeded roll and the numbers as data rows; keep the per-run counts in the one character ledger and count tokens at generation. The strength and enchant curves are also worth keeping as fixed formulas; only the token schedule needs to be a row.", "decision_status":"proposed", "acceptance":"Server test with a fixed seed over 40 generated levels: every forced life token satisfies 4 x (tokens so far) + 3 < depth + offset, the offset stays within -2..2, and a strength token appears at a rate within 10 percent of the row's target."}
